IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `rtw-dates`
IMPORT `rtw-core`

-- Return to Work Act 2014 (SA), with the Return to Work Regulations 2015 -- the injured worker's questions.
--
-- SEAT: the injured worker (and, after a death from a work injury, the worker's partner, children and the person who
-- paid for the funeral). Every question is phrased as that person asks it: "Am I a worker?", "Is my injury a work
-- injury?", "By when must I give notice and claim?", "What weekly payment do I get, and until when?", "Am I a seriously
-- injured worker?", "What lump sum do I get?", "Must my employer give me work?", "May I sue my employer?". The rules are in
-- rtw-core.l4; this module builds the core's records from plain answers and restates no rule. Its names differ from the
-- employer seat's (rtw-seat-employer.l4), so a case file can import both.
--
-- Amounts marked "(indexed)" take two CPI figures (Adelaide, All groups, September quarters), which are not deposited;
-- see NOTES.md. Edition: the Open Australian Legal Corpus texts as at 2024-12-01 (scraped 2025-03-10); they may be out of
-- date.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Return to Work Act 2014 (SA) -- the injured worker's questions`

§§ `Am I covered (s 4, regs 5 and 6; s 7)`

@export Am I a worker under the Return to Work Act 2014 (SA) (s 4(1), (2); Return to Work Regulations 2015 regs 5 and 6)?
GIVEN `I am employed by the person I work for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are employed by the person you do the work for (a contract of employment)
      `I am an apprentice or trainee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you work under a contract of apprenticeship, including as a trainee under the South Australian Skills Act 2008
      `I am paid while I get on-the-job training from them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person you work for gives you on-the-job training in a trade or vocation and pays you during it
      `the kind of work I do` IS A `Prescribed class of work` @desc Whether your work is one of the kinds the regulations bring in (reg 5): building work other than tiling, window cleaning, other cleaning, driving under a local government award, taxi driving without the licence, driving or riding a non-commercial vehicle to deliver goods, entertaining at a venue, thoroughbred riding as a licensed jockey, award outwork, or the work of a minister or member of a religious order; otherwise none of them
      `I do it for their trade or business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you do the work in the course of, or for the purposes of, a trade or business carried on by the person you work for
      `I do the work personally` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you do the work yourself (whether or not you supply tools or equipment)
      `I employ someone to do part of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you employ anyone else to do any part of the work
      `the materials I supply are worth` IS A NUMBER @desc The value in dollars of the materials you supply, or are expected to supply, under the arrangement (0 if none)
      `the whole job pays` IS A NUMBER @desc The total in dollars payable, or expected to be payable, to you under the arrangement (only matters for building work)
      `my most valuable tool is worth` IS A NUMBER @desc The price in dollars of a new equivalent of your most valuable single tool or item of plant or equipment owned or leased for work (only matters for building work)
      `the arrangement lasts this many months` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months the arrangement runs for (only matters for cleaning work; 1 for a month or less)
      `I run more than 1 vehicle for work at once` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you own or operate more than one vehicle for work at the same time (only matters for delivery driving or riding)
      `the goods are or were mine or theirs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the goods you carry are, or were ever, owned by you or by the person you work for (only matters for delivery work)
      `they or someone related supply my vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your vehicle is owned by, leased or hired from, or otherwise supplied by the person you work for or someone related to them (only matters if you drive your own commercial vehicle)
      `I am fishing crew paid by a share` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a member of the crew of a fishing boat paid by a share of the profits or gross receipts from working the boat
      `I am a volunteer of a prescribed class` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a volunteer of a class of whom the Crown is the presumptive employer, such as a Country Fire Service member doing CFS work (Act Schedule 1)
      `the Corporation has extended cover to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether ReturnToWorkSA (the Corporation) has extended the Act's protection to you as a self-employed person (s 175)
      `my regulation 6 class` IS A `Regulation 6 class` @desc Whether you are in a class the regulations exclude (reg 6): a minister, priest, pastor or deaconess of the churches named in reg 6(1); a contestant employed for a sporting or athletic activity (but not a licensed race rider or driver, or a boxer or wrestler engaged for a fee); a driver carrying goods in a commercial motor vehicle you own, lease or hire; a person covered by the Seafarers Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 1992; otherwise none
      `the CPI for the latest September quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc The Consumer Price Index (All groups, Adelaide) for the September quarter of last year, used to index the dollar limits in reg 5
      `the CPI for the September quarter of 2014` IS A NUMBER @desc The Consumer Price Index (All groups, Adelaide) for the September quarter of 2014, the base for reg 5's dollar limits
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a worker` IF
    `the person is a worker`
        (`Engagement facts` WITH
            `employed by the other person`                                             IS `I am employed by the person I work for`
            `an apprentice or trainee under a contract of apprenticeship`              IS `I am an apprentice or trainee`
            `paid while receiving on-the-job training in a trade or vocation from the other person` IS `I am paid while I get on-the-job training from them`
            `the class of work`                                                        IS `the kind of work I do`
            `the work is done for the purposes of the other person's trade or business` IS `I do it for their trade or business`
            `the work is done personally`                                              IS `I do the work personally`
            `someone else is employed to do part of the work`                          IS `I employ someone to do part of it`
            `the value of the materials supplied`                                      IS `the materials I supply are worth`
            `the total payable under the arrangement`                                  IS `the whole job pays`
            `the value of the most valuable tool or item of plant or equipment`        IS `my most valuable tool is worth`
            `the term of the arrangement in months`                                    IS `the arrangement lasts this many months`
            `more than 1 vehicle is owned or operated for work at the same time`       IS `I run more than 1 vehicle for work at once`
            `the goods are or were owned by the driver or by the other person`         IS `the goods are or were mine or theirs`
            `the vehicle is supplied by the other person or someone related to it`     IS `they or someone related supply my vehicle`
            `a fishing crew member paid by a share of profits or gross receipts`       IS `I am fishing crew paid by a share`
            `a volunteer of whom the Crown is the presumptive employer under Schedule 1` IS `I am a volunteer of a prescribed class`
            `the Corporation has extended the Act's protection to the person under s 175` IS `the Corporation has extended cover to me`
            `the regulation 6 class`                                                   IS `my regulation 6 class`)
        (`CPI figures` WITH
            `the CPI for the September quarter before the adjustment` IS `the CPI for the latest September quarter`
            `the CPI for the base September quarter`                 IS `the CPI for the September quarter of 2014`)

@export My employer is a contractor working for someone else: is that principal taken to be my employer (s 4(4), reg 5(8))?
GIVEN `the principal contracted my employer for work the principal took on` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person your employer contracts with (the principal) contracted your employer to do work that the principal itself had undertaken
      `my employer is registered as an employer under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer (the contractor) is registered as an employer with ReturnToWorkSA
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the principal taken to be my employer` IF
    `the principal is taken to be the employer of the contractor's workers` `the principal contracted my employer for work the principal took on` `my employer is registered as an employer under the Act`

@export Does my injury arise from employment, so that the Act applies to it (s 7)?
GIVEN `my injury is` IS A `Kind of injury` @desc Whether your injury is a physical injury, or a psychiatric injury (pure mental harm, not mental harm that follows a bodily injury)
      `it happened out of or in the course of my work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury arose out of, or in the course of, your employment
      `work was a significant contributing cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employment was a significant contributing cause of the injury (the test for a physical injury)
      `work was the significant contributing cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employment was the significant contributing cause of the injury (the test for a psychiatric injury)
      `it came mainly from reasonable management action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a psychiatric injury: whether it arose wholly or predominantly from reasonable action taken in a reasonable manner to transfer, demote, discipline, counsel, retrench or dismiss you, a reasonable decision not to promote or give a benefit, reasonable administrative action, or reasonable action under the Act
      `it happened at a social or sporting activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury arose from your involvement in a social or sporting activity
      `the activity was part of my job or my employer asked me to go` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that activity was part of your employment, or undertaken at your employer's direction or request
      `it happened on a journey` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury arose out of or in the course of a journey
      `the journey was part of my duties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the journey was undertaken in the course of carrying out your duties
      `the journey was between home or work and a listed place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the journey was between your residence and your place of employment, or between either of them and a place of training you must or may attend, or a place for medical services, return to work services or a compensation claim
      `I took a reasonably direct route` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you took a reasonably direct route, with no substantial interruption or deviation that materially increased the risk of injury
      `there is a real and substantial connection between my work and the journey` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there was a real and substantial connection between your employment and the journey at the time of the accident (having an accident on the way to or from work is not enough on its own)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my injury a work injury` IF
    `the injury arises from employment`
        (`Injury facts` WITH
            `the kind of injury`                                                     IS `my injury is`
            `it arose out of or in the course of employment`                         IS `it happened out of or in the course of my work`
            `employment was a significant contributing cause`                        IS `work was a significant contributing cause`
            `employment was the significant contributing cause`                      IS `work was the significant contributing cause`
            `it arose wholly or predominantly from reasonable action or decisions of the kinds in s 7(4)` IS `it came mainly from reasonable management action`
            `it arose from a social or sporting activity`                            IS `it happened at a social or sporting activity`
            `the activity was part of the employment or at the employer's direction or request` IS `the activity was part of my job or my employer asked me to go`
            `it arose on a journey`                                                  IS `it happened on a journey`
            `the journey was in the course of carrying out duties of employment`     IS `the journey was part of my duties`
            `the journey was between places listed in s 7(8)(b)`                     IS `the journey was between home or work and a listed place`
            `the route was reasonably direct without a substantial, riskier deviation` IS `I took a reasonably direct route`
            `there is a real and substantial connection between the employment and the journey` IS `there is a real and substantial connection between my work and the journey`)

§§ `Notice of my injury, and my claim (ss 16, 30, 31, 32; regs 11, 19)`

@export To whom must I give notice of my work injury (s 16(1))?
GIVEN `I was employed when I was injured` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were employed by an employer at the time of the injury
      `I am self-employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are self-employed (covered by ReturnToWorkSA as a self-employed worker)
GIVETH A `Notice recipient`
DECIDE `To whom must I give notice of my injury` IS
    `to whom notice of the injury must be given` `I was employed when I was injured` `I am self-employed`

@export Within how many hours of my injury should I give notice of it (s 16(2))?
GIVEN `I could practicably give notice within 24 hours` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was practicable to give notice within 24 hours of the injury (or of becoming aware of it, if you were not aware of it straight away)
      `the hours within which it was practicable` IS A NUMBER @desc If 24 hours was not practicable: how many hours after the injury (or after you became aware of it) it first became practicable to give notice
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Within how many hours should I give notice of my injury` IS
    `the hours within which notice should be given` `I could practicably give notice within 24 hours` `the hours within which it was practicable`

@export Is the notice I gave taken to have been given to my employer (s 16(4), reg 11)?
GIVEN `how I gave notice` IS A `Manner of giving notice` @desc How you gave notice: to your employer at its place of business; to the person supervising you when you were injured; to a person your employer designated; by post to your employer; by email to an address your employer uses for its business; or some other way
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my notice taken to have been given to my employer` IF
    `notice given this way is taken to have been given to the employer` `how I gave notice`

@export What is the last day for me to make my claim (s 30(1)(b), (10))?
GIVEN `the day my entitlement to claim arose` IS A DATE @desc The day your entitlement to make the claim arose, such as the first day you were incapacitated for work or the day a cost was incurred (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-03-03)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `What is the last day to make my claim` IS
    `the last day to make the claim` `the day my entitlement to claim arose`

@export Can I still make my claim, given when I claim and whether I gave notice of the injury (s 30(1)-(3))?
GIVEN `the day my entitlement to claim arose` IS A DATE @desc The day your entitlement to make the claim arose (ISO 8601)
      `the day I give my claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you give, or gave, your claim to your employer or ReturnToWorkSA (ISO 8601)
      `I gave notice of my injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you gave notice of the injury to your employer (or ReturnToWorkSA if you were not employed)
      `the delay or missing notice has not substantially prejudiced the claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the proper determination of your claim has not been substantially prejudiced by a late claim or a missing notice (a judgment for ReturnToWorkSA or the Tribunal)
      `I failed to give notice through ignorance, mistake, absence or other reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you gave no notice: whether that was because of your ignorance, a mistake, your absence from South Australia, or another reasonable cause
      `I claimed late through ignorance, mistake, absence or other reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your claim is late: whether that was because of your ignorance, a mistake, your absence from South Australia, or another reasonable cause
GIVETH A `Claim answer`
DECIDE `Can I still make my claim` IS
    `the s 30 answer for`
        (`Claim facts` WITH
            `the day the entitlement to make the claim arose`                           IS `the day my entitlement to claim arose`
            `the day the claim was given`                                              IS `the day I give my claim`
            `notice of the injury was given`                                           IS `I gave notice of my injury`
            `the proper determination of the claim has not been substantially prejudiced` IS `the delay or missing notice has not substantially prejudiced the claim`
            `the failure to give notice came from ignorance, mistake, absence from the State or other reasonable cause` IS `I failed to give notice through ignorance, mistake, absence or other reasonable cause`
            `the lateness came from ignorance, mistake, absence from the State or other reasonable cause` IS `I claimed late through ignorance, mistake, absence or other reasonable cause`)

@export To whom must I give my claim (s 30(4))?
GIVEN `I was employed when my incapacity began` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were in employment when your incapacity for work began
GIVETH A `Claim recipient`
DECIDE `To whom must I give my claim` IS
    `to whom the claim must be given` `I was employed when my incapacity began`

@export Who can sign the certificate that must support my claim (s 30(1)(c), (10); reg 19)?
GIVEN `who signs it` IS A `Certifier` @desc Who would sign the certificate: a recognised health practitioner (a medical practitioner, or a health practitioner ReturnToWorkSA recognises for this kind of injury); a nurse practitioner who examined you at an incorporated or private hospital; or someone else
GIVETH A `Certificate answer`
DECIDE `Who can certify my claim` IS
    `who may certify the claim` `who signs it`

@export By when must my employer forward my claim to ReturnToWorkSA (s 30(5))?
GIVEN `I was employed when my incapacity began` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were in employment when your incapacity for work began (if not, the claim goes straight to ReturnToWorkSA)
      `the day my employer received my claim` IS A DATE @desc The day your employer received your claim (ISO 8601)
      `weekday public holidays in the next 5 business days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many South Australian public holidays fall on a Monday to Friday in the 5 business days after that day (each one adds a business day); the day your employer received the claim is not counted, so a holiday on that day is not one of them
      `my employer is self-insured` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer is registered with ReturnToWorkSA as a self-insured employer
GIVETH A `Forwarding answer`
DECIDE `By when must my employer forward my claim` IS
    `the s 30(4), (5) answer for a claim, in employment when the incapacity commenced` `I was employed when my incapacity began` `received on` `the day my employer received my claim` `with public holidays` `weekday public holidays in the next 5 business days` `self-insured` `my employer is self-insured`

@export By what day should ReturnToWorkSA try to decide my claim for income support, after which it must offer me interim payments (s 31(4), s 32(2))?
GIVEN `the day ReturnToWorkSA received my claim` IS A DATE @desc The day ReturnToWorkSA (the Corporation) received your claim for weekly payments (ISO 8601)
      `weekday public holidays in the next 10 business days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many South Australian public holidays fall on a Monday to Friday in the 10 business days after that day (each one adds a business day); the day ReturnToWorkSA received the claim is not counted, so a holiday on that day is not one of them
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when should my income support claim be decided` IS
    `the 10th business day after the Corporation received the claim on` `the day ReturnToWorkSA received my claim` `with public holidays` `weekday public holidays in the next 10 business days`

§§ `My weekly payments (ss 5, 36-44; regs 7, 9, 26, 27)`

@export What are my average weekly earnings under the Act (s 5; regs 7, 9)?
GIVEN `my earnings in the period, leaving out overtime` IS A NUMBER @desc What you earned from all your employers in the 12 months before the injury (or the shorter period the Act uses for you), including leave pay and salary you sacrificed into superannuation, but leaving out overtime, your employer's superannuation contributions and occasional travel or accommodation allowances, in dollars
      `the weeks in that period` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of weeks in that period (52 for a full 12 months)
      `the weekly value of non-cash benefits I lose` IS A NUMBER @desc The weekly value in dollars of non-cash benefits of the kinds in reg 9 (a car, housing or accommodation, school fees, health insurance, a phone, a computer, internet, a staff discount, a credit card, a cheap loan, medical benefits) that you do not keep while off work
      `I could reasonably expect overtime` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on the day of the injury, you had a reasonable expectation of working overtime in the foreseeable future
      `the overtime component of my earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc The weekly overtime component in dollars worked out under s 5(12)(b) (its formula is missing from the text this encoding uses, so give the figure ReturnToWorkSA worked out)
      `an award or agreement covered my pay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your pay was covered by an award or industrial agreement on the day of the injury
      `my weekly award wage` IS A NUMBER @desc The weekly wage you were entitled to under that award or agreement, in dollars (0 if none)
      `I am a self-employed worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are covered as a self-employed worker
      `my usual weekly hours` IS A NUMBER @desc The hours a week you were working on the day of the injury
      `full-time weekly hours in my kind of work` IS A NUMBER @desc The hours a week that are full-time employment in your kind of work (for example 38)
      `the Federal minimum wage per week` IS A NUMBER @desc The weekly national minimum wage that applied to you under the Fair Work Act 2009 national minimum wage order, in dollars
      `State average weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc The Australian Bureau of Statistics' last published estimate before the day of the injury of Average Weekly Earnings for ordinary hours of each full-time employed adult male in South Australia, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What are my average weekly earnings` IS
    `the average weekly earnings under s 5`
        (`Earnings facts` WITH
            `the earnings in the relevant period, other than overtime`         IS `my earnings in the period, leaving out overtime`
            `the weeks in the relevant period`                                 IS `the weeks in that period`
            `the weekly value of prescribed non-cash benefits not retained`     IS `the weekly value of non-cash benefits I lose`
            `a reasonable expectation of working overtime`                     IS `I could reasonably expect overtime`
            `the overtime component`                                           IS `the overtime component of my earnings`
            `the pay was covered by an award or industrial agreement`          IS `an award or agreement covered my pay`
            `the weekly wage under the award or industrial agreement`          IS `my weekly award wage`
            `a self-employed worker`                                           IS `I am a self-employed worker`
            `the hours worked per week`                                        IS `my usual weekly hours`
            `the hours per week that constitute full-time employment`          IS `full-time weekly hours in my kind of work`
            `the Federal minimum wage per week`                                IS `the Federal minimum wage per week`
            `State average weekly earnings`                                    IS `State average weekly earnings`)

@export Do I have a current work capacity, no current work capacity, or no incapacity for work (s 36)?
GIVEN `I can go back to my pre-injury job` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are able to return to the employment you had when you were injured
      `I can do suitable work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are able to work in suitable employment: work you are currently suited to, given your injury, age, skills, experience, where you live and the medical information
GIVETH A `Work capacity`
DECIDE `What is my work capacity` IS
    `the work capacity of a worker` `I can go back to my pre-injury job` `I can do suitable work`

@export What weekly payment do I get for a day of incapacity (ss 39, 41, 42, 44)?
GIVEN `I am a seriously injured worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a seriously injured worker (assessed at 35% or more whole person impairment for a physical injury, or 30% or more for a psychiatric injury, or taken to be one by an interim decision)
      `I can go back to my pre-injury job` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are able to return to the employment you had when you were injured
      `I can do suitable work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are able to work in suitable employment
      `the first day of my incapacity` IS A DATE @desc The first day for which you were entitled to weekly payments for this incapacity (ISO 8601)
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc A day in the week you are asking about (ISO 8601)
      `my notional weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc Your notional weekly earnings in dollars: your average weekly earnings, as adjusted by ReturnToWorkSA, but not more than twice State average weekly earnings
      `what I now earn a week` IS A NUMBER @desc What you now earn a week in employment or self-employment, in dollars, leaving out leave pay, retirement, superannuation and redundancy payments, and allowances (0 if not working)
      `the Federal minimum wage per week` IS A NUMBER @desc The weekly national minimum wage that applies to you, in dollars
      `my usual weekly hours` IS A NUMBER @desc The hours a week you were working on the day of the injury
      `full-time weekly hours in my kind of work` IS A NUMBER @desc The hours a week that are full-time employment in your kind of work
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth (ISO 8601)
      `my kind of work has a normal retiring age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is a normal retiring age for workers in the kind of employment you were injured in
      `that retiring age in months` IS A NUMBER @desc That normal retiring age, in months (for example 780 for 65); 0 if none
      `my age pension age in months` IS A NUMBER @desc The age, in months, at which you would be eligible for the age pension under the Social Security Act 1991 (Cth) (804, which is 67, for anyone born on or after 1 January 1957)
      `I was employed when my incapacity began` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were still in employment when your incapacity for work first began
GIVETH A `Weekly payment answer`
DECIDE `What weekly payment do I get` IS
    `the weekly payment on the day for`
        (`Weekly payment facts` WITH
            `paid as a seriously injured worker`        IS `I am a seriously injured worker`
            `the work capacity`                         IS `the work capacity of a worker` `I can go back to my pre-injury job` `I can do suitable work`
            `the day incapacity first occurred`          IS `the first day of my incapacity`
            `the day asked about`                        IS `the day I am asking about`
            `notional weekly earnings`                   IS `my notional weekly earnings`
            `designated weekly earnings`                 IS `what I now earn a week`
            `the Federal minimum wage for the worker`    IS `the Federal minimum wage for` `my usual weekly hours` `hours of` `full-time weekly hours in my kind of work` `from` `the Federal minimum wage per week`)
        `with retiring age facts`
        (`Retiring age facts` WITH
            `the date of birth`                                           IS `my date of birth`
            `there is a normal retiring age for the kind of employment`   IS `my kind of work has a normal retiring age`
            `the normal retiring age, in months`                          IS `that retiring age in months`
            `the age pension age, in months`                              IS `my age pension age in months`
            `the day incapacity first occurred`                           IS `the first day of my incapacity`
            `still in employment when the incapacity first occurred`      IS `I was employed when my incapacity began`)

@export Until what day can I be paid weekly payments (ss 39(3), 41, 44)?
GIVEN `I am a seriously injured worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a seriously injured worker
      `the first day of my incapacity` IS A DATE @desc The first day for which you were entitled to weekly payments for this incapacity (ISO 8601)
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth (ISO 8601)
      `my kind of work has a normal retiring age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is a normal retiring age for workers in the kind of employment you were injured in
      `that retiring age in months` IS A NUMBER @desc That normal retiring age, in months; 0 if none
      `my age pension age in months` IS A NUMBER @desc The age, in months, at which you would be eligible for the age pension under the Social Security Act 1991 (Cth)
      `I was employed when my incapacity began` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were still in employment when your incapacity for work first began
GIVETH A `Retiring age answer`
DECIDE `Until when can I get weekly payments` IS
    `the last day of weekly payments for`
        (`Retiring age facts` WITH
            `the date of birth`                                           IS `my date of birth`
            `there is a normal retiring age for the kind of employment`   IS `my kind of work has a normal retiring age`
            `the normal retiring age, in months`                          IS `that retiring age in months`
            `the age pension age, in months`                              IS `my age pension age in months`
            `the day incapacity first occurred`                           IS `the first day of my incapacity`
            `still in employment when the incapacity first occurred`      IS `I was employed when my incapacity began`)
        `if seriously injured` `I am a seriously injured worker`

-- Situation: the worker was paid as a seriously injured worker and an assessment then found otherwise.
@export An assessment found I am not a seriously injured worker after all: am I still paid as one on this day (s 41(3))?
GIVEN `the day of the assessment` IS A DATE @desc The date of the whole person impairment assessment that found you are not a seriously injured worker (ISO 8601)
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about (ISO 8601)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I still paid as a seriously injured worker` IF
    `the day is within 8 weeks of the assessment` `the day of the assessment` `the day I am asking about`

-- Situation: the worker has had surgery after the first 104 weeks.
@export What supplementary income support do I get for incapacity after surgery, once the 104 weeks are over (s 40, reg 26)?
GIVEN `I can go back to my pre-injury job` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are able to return to the employment you had when you were injured
      `I can do suitable work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are able to work in suitable employment
      `the first day of my incapacity` IS A DATE @desc The first day for which you were entitled to weekly payments for this injury (ISO 8601)
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc A day of incapacity you are asking about (ISO 8601)
      `the surgery was approved by ReturnToWorkSA` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether ReturnToWorkSA approved the surgery
      `the day of the surgery` IS A DATE @desc The day of the surgery (ISO 8601)
      `my notional weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc Your notional weekly earnings in dollars
      `what I now earn a week` IS A NUMBER @desc What you now earn a week in employment or self-employment, in dollars (0 if not working)
      `the Federal minimum wage per week` IS A NUMBER @desc The weekly national minimum wage that applies to you, in dollars
      `my usual weekly hours` IS A NUMBER @desc The hours a week you were working on the day of the injury
      `full-time weekly hours in my kind of work` IS A NUMBER @desc The hours a week that are full-time employment in your kind of work
      `the CPI two quarters before the payments start` IS A NUMBER @desc The Consumer Price Index (All groups, Adelaide) for the quarter falling 2 quarters before the supplementary payments start
      `the CPI for the quarter before my 104 weeks ended` IS A NUMBER @desc The Consumer Price Index (All groups, Adelaide) for the quarter immediately before the quarter in which your 104 weeks (second designated period) ended
GIVETH A `Supplementary answer`
DECIDE `What supplementary income support do I get` IS
    `the s 40 payment for`
        (`Supplementary facts` WITH
            `the weekly facts` IS
                (`Weekly payment facts` WITH
                    `paid as a seriously injured worker`        IS FALSE  -- s 40 is for a worker not paid under s 41; this field is not read by s 40
                    `the work capacity`                         IS `the work capacity of a worker` `I can go back to my pre-injury job` `I can do suitable work`
                    `the day incapacity first occurred`          IS `the first day of my incapacity`
                    `the day asked about`                        IS `the day I am asking about`
                    `notional weekly earnings`                   IS `my notional weekly earnings`
                    `designated weekly earnings`                 IS `what I now earn a week`
                    `the Federal minimum wage for the worker`    IS `the Federal minimum wage for` `my usual weekly hours` `hours of` `full-time weekly hours in my kind of work` `from` `the Federal minimum wage per week`)
            `the surgery was approved by the Corporation` IS `the surgery was approved by ReturnToWorkSA`
            `the day of the surgery`                    IS `the day of the surgery`)
        `with`
        (`CPI figures` WITH
            `the CPI for the September quarter before the adjustment` IS `the CPI two quarters before the payments start`
            `the CPI for the base September quarter`                 IS `the CPI for the quarter before my 104 weeks ended`)

@export On what day of a year is the Federal minimum wage in my weekly payments adjusted (s 42(3), reg 27)?
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER @desc The year (for example 2026)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `When is the minimum wage in my payments adjusted` IS
    `the day the s 42 Federal minimum wage is adjusted in` `the year`

@export Must I make reasonable efforts to return to work (s 43(1))?
GIVEN `I can go back to my pre-injury job` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are able to return to the employment you had when you were injured
      `I can do suitable work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are able to work in suitable employment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I make reasonable efforts to return to work` IF
    `s 43(1) binds a worker with` (`the work capacity of a worker` `I can go back to my pre-injury job` `I can do suitable work`)

@export Am I treated as making reasonable efforts to return to work while I wait (s 43(2))?
GIVEN `I am waiting for return to work services in my plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, for a reasonable period, you are waiting for recovery/return to work services your plan requires to start
      `I am waiting for my employer to answer my request for work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, for a reasonable period, you are waiting for your employer's response to a request for work that it received
      `I am waiting for work my employer said it will give me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, for a reasonable period, you are waiting for work your employer has said it will provide to start
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I treated as making reasonable efforts` IF
    `the worker is treated as making reasonable efforts to return to work` `I am waiting for return to work services in my plan` `I am waiting for my employer to answer my request for work` `I am waiting for work my employer said it will give me`

§§ `Am I a seriously injured worker (s 21)`

@export Am I a seriously injured worker (s 21)?
GIVEN `my whole person impairment from physical injury` IS A NUMBER @desc Your degree of whole person impairment from physical injury, in per cent, as assessed by an accredited medical practitioner under s 22 (0 if none)
      `my whole person impairment from psychiatric injury` IS A NUMBER @desc Your degree of whole person impairment from psychiatric injury, in per cent, assessed separately (0 if none)
      `my final examination was on or after the 2022 designated day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the accredited medical practitioner's final examination for your assessment was on or after the designated day proclaimed under the Return to Work (Scheme Sustainability) Amendment Act 2022 (the day is not in the text this encoding uses)
      `I have an interim decision in my favour` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether ReturnToWorkSA has made an interim decision, still in effect, that you are taken to be a seriously injured worker pending your assessment
GIVETH A `Seriously injured answer`
DECIDE `Am I a seriously injured worker` IS
    `the s 21 answer for`
        (`Impairment facts` WITH
            `the whole person impairment from physical injury, in per cent`     IS `my whole person impairment from physical injury`
            `the whole person impairment from psychiatric injury, in per cent`  IS `my whole person impairment from psychiatric injury`
            `the final examination was on or after the 2022 designated day`     IS `my final examination was on or after the 2022 designated day`)
        `with an interim decision` `I have an interim decision in my favour`

§§ `Suitable work from my employer (s 18, reg 12)`

-- Situation: the worker was incapacitated and can now return to work.
@export Must my pre-injury employer give me suitable work (s 18(1), (2))?
GIVEN `I was incapacitated by a work injury from this job` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were incapacitated for work by a work injury that arose from your employment with this employer
      `I am able to return to work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are now able to return to work, full-time or part-time, in your old job or another (including because you are no longer incapacitated)
      `my employer has shown it is not reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer has established that it is not reasonably practicable to provide you with suitable employment
      `I left this employer before my incapacity began` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had left this employer before your incapacity for work began
      `I ended the employment after my incapacity began` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you yourself ended the employment after your incapacity began
      `my employer has shown I was properly dismissed for serious and wilful misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer has established that your employment was properly terminated for serious and wilful misconduct
      `I agreed to other employment options in my plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you agreed to new or other employment options under s 25(10a)
      `I have already returned to work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have otherwise returned to work with this employer or another employer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my employer give me suitable work` IF
    `the pre-injury employer must provide suitable employment`
        (`Suitable work facts` WITH
            `the worker was incapacitated for work by a work injury from this employment` IS `I was incapacitated by a work injury from this job`
            `the worker is able to return to work`                                    IS `I am able to return to work`
            `the employer has established it is not reasonably practicable`           IS `my employer has shown it is not reasonably practicable`
            `the worker left this employer before the incapacity began`               IS `I left this employer before my incapacity began`
            `the worker ended the employment after the incapacity began`              IS `I ended the employment after my incapacity began`
            `the employer has established a proper termination for serious and wilful misconduct` IS `my employer has shown I was properly dismissed for serious and wilful misconduct`
            `the worker agreed to other employment options under s 25(10a)`           IS `I agreed to other employment options in my plan`
            `the worker has otherwise returned to work`                               IS `I have already returned to work`)

@export Is my notice to my employer asking for work a valid subsection (3) notice (s 18(3), (4))?
GIVEN `it is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your notice to your employer is in writing
      `it says I am ready, willing and able to return` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it confirms that you are ready, willing and able to return to work with the employer
      `it says what work I think I can do` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it gives information about the type of work you consider you are capable of doing
      `I was a labour hire worker seeking the host's help` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a labour hire worker injured while supplied to a host employer, and you want the host to cooperate in giving you work
      `it asks for the host's cooperation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the notice contains a statement that you seek the host employer's cooperation
      `it comes with evidence of my capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the notice is supported by evidence of your capacity for work (such as a medical certificate)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my notice a subsection (3) notice` IF
    `the notice is a subsection (3) notice` `it is in writing` `it says I am ready, willing and able to return` `it says what work I think I can do` `I was a labour hire worker seeking the host's help` `it asks for the host's cooperation` `it comes with evidence of my capacity`

@export Must I also give the host employer a copy of my subsection (3) notice and the evidence, as soon as reasonably practicable (s 18(4a))?
GIVEN `I was a labour hire worker when injured` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a labour hire worker at the time of the work injury
      `I was supplied to a host employer when injured` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury arose from employment while you were supplied to a host employer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I give the host employer a copy of my notice` IF
    `s 18(4a) applies to a worker who was` `I was a labour hire worker when injured` `and` `I was supplied to a host employer when injured`

@export By when must my employer answer my subsection (3) notice in writing (s 18(4b))?
GIVEN `the day my employer received my notice` IS A DATE @desc The day your pre-injury employer received your subsection (3) notice (ISO 8601)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must my employer answer my notice` IS
    `the last day for the employer's written reply to a notice received on` `the day my employer received my notice`

@export By when may I apply to the Tribunal for an order that my employer give me work (s 18(4d), (4e))?
GIVEN `the day my employer received my notice` IS A DATE @desc The day your pre-injury employer received your subsection (3) notice (ISO 8601)
      `my employer answered in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer gave you its written answer
      `the day of my employer's answer` IS A DATE @desc The day your employer gave its written answer (ISO 8601; any date if it has not answered)
      `I was no longer incapacitated when I gave the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had already ceased to be incapacitated for work by the injury when you gave the notice
      `the day I ceased to be incapacitated` IS A DATE @desc The day you ceased to be incapacitated for work (ISO 8601; any date if you have not)
GIVETH A `Tribunal window answer`
DECIDE `By when may I apply to the Tribunal for work` IS
    `the s 18(4d) window for`
        (`Subsection (3) timing facts` WITH
            `the day the employer received the subsection (3) notice`            IS `the day my employer received my notice`
            `the employer gave a written reply`                                  IS `my employer answered in writing`
            `the day of the employer's written reply`                            IS `the day of my employer's answer`
            `the worker had ceased to be incapacitated when giving the notice`   IS `I was no longer incapacitated when I gave the notice`
            `the day the worker ceased to be incapacitated`                      IS `the day I ceased to be incapacitated`)

@export What is the most I can be awarded in costs for a stage of my application about suitable work (s 18(6), (7); reg 12)?
GIVEN `the stage` IS A `Stage of the s 18 proceedings` @desc The stage of the proceedings: preparing and lodging the application; taking part up to and including a pre-hearing conference; the same where the Tribunal determines you are entitled to more; or proceedings after a pre-hearing conference
      `the Supreme Court scale amount` IS A NUMBER @desc For proceedings after a pre-hearing conference: the costs allowable under the relevant Supreme Court scale, in dollars (0 otherwise)
      `the CPI for the latest September quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc The Consumer Price Index (All groups, Adelaide) for the September quarter of last year
      `the CPI for the September quarter of 2014` IS A NUMBER @desc The Consumer Price Index (All groups, Adelaide) for the September quarter of 2014
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be awarded in costs` IS
    `the reg 12 costs limit for` `the stage` `with a Supreme Court scale amount of` `the Supreme Court scale amount` `and`
        (`CPI figures` WITH
            `the CPI for the September quarter before the adjustment` IS `the CPI for the latest September quarter`
            `the CPI for the base September quarter`                 IS `the CPI for the September quarter of 2014`)

§§ `If my employer wants to end my employment (s 20)`

-- Situation: the employer proposes to end the injured worker's employment.
@export Must my employer give me and ReturnToWorkSA 28 days notice before ending my employment (s 20)?
GIVEN `my work injury arose in this job` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you suffered a work injury that arose from your employment with this employer
      `my employer has shown serious and wilful misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer has established that the employment is properly ended for serious and wilful misconduct
      `I am in a return to work plan or getting compensation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are participating in a recovery/return to work plan, or receiving compensation, for the injury
      `my rights are exhausted or my time to claim has passed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your rights to compensation for the injury are exhausted, or the time for making a claim has expired
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my employer give me notice before ending my employment` IF
    `s 20 notice is required before terminating`
        (`Termination facts` WITH
            `the worker suffered a work injury in this employment`               IS `my work injury arose in this job`
            `a proper termination for serious and wilful misconduct, established by the employer` IS `my employer has shown serious and wilful misconduct`
            `the worker is in a recovery/return to work plan or receiving compensation for the injury` IS `I am in a return to work plan or getting compensation`
            `the worker's rights to compensation are exhausted or the time to claim has expired` IS `my rights are exhausted or my time to claim has passed`)

@export If my employer gives notice of a proposed termination, what is the earliest day my employment can end (s 20(1))?
GIVEN `the day notice was given` IS A DATE @desc The day your employer gave you and ReturnToWorkSA notice of the proposed termination (ISO 8601)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `What is the earliest day my employment can end` IS
    `the earliest day the employment may end after notice on` `the day notice was given`

§§ `Medical expenses and damaged property (ss 33, 35; regs 23, 25)`

@export Is a medical cost I incur on a given day still covered, or has my entitlement to medical expenses ended (s 33(20), (21); reg 23)?
GIVEN `I am a seriously injured worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a seriously injured worker
      `the day of my injury` IS A DATE @desc The day of the injury (ISO 8601)
      `I have had an entitlement to weekly payments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have ever been entitled to weekly payments for this injury
      `the last day of my weekly payment entitlement` IS A DATE @desc The last day of your entitlement to weekly payments (ISO 8601; any date if you have never had one)
      `the kind of cost` IS A `Kind of medical cost` @desc The kind of cost: an ordinary medical cost; a therapeutic appliance needed to maintain your capacity; later surgery ReturnToWorkSA accepted on an application made before the period ended; services ReturnToWorkSA accepted, on an application made before the period ended, for a cancer or silica injury listed in reg 23(1); or travel and accommodation to attend a permanent impairment assessment
      `the day of the cost` IS A DATE @desc The day the cost is incurred (ISO 8601)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my medical cost still covered` IF
    `the cost is within the period for medical expenses`
        (`Medical period facts` WITH
            `a seriously injured worker`                         IS `I am a seriously injured worker`
            `the day of the injury`                              IS `the day of my injury`
            `there was an entitlement to weekly payments`        IS `I have had an entitlement to weekly payments`
            `the last day of the entitlement to weekly payments` IS `the last day of my weekly payment entitlement`
            `the kind of cost`                                   IS `the kind of cost`
            `the day the cost is incurred`                       IS `the day of the cost`)

@export How much do I get for property damaged when I was injured (s 35, reg 25)?
GIVEN `damage to my therapeutic appliances and tools of trade` IS A NUMBER @desc The cost in dollars of the damage to your therapeutic appliances (glasses, hearing aids, dentures, prostheses and similar) and tools of trade (not a motor vehicle)
      `damage to my clothes and personal effects` IS A NUMBER @desc The cost in dollars of the damage to your clothes and personal effects
      `the CPI for the latest September quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc The Consumer Price Index (All groups, Adelaide) for the September quarter of the year before the year of the injury
      `the CPI for the September quarter of 2014` IS A NUMBER @desc The Consumer Price Index (All groups, Adelaide) for the September quarter of 2014
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much do I get for damaged property` IS
    `the property damage compensation for` `damage to my therapeutic appliances and tools of trade` `and` `damage to my clothes and personal effects` `with`
        (`CPI figures` WITH
            `the CPI for the September quarter before the adjustment` IS `the CPI for the latest September quarter`
            `the CPI for the base September quarter`                 IS `the CPI for the September quarter of 2014`)

§§ `If my weekly payments are cut or stopped (s 48, reg 28)`

-- Situation: ReturnToWorkSA has decided to reduce or discontinue the worker's weekly payments.
@export How much notice must I get before my weekly payments are reduced or stopped (s 48(6), (7), (10a))?
GIVEN `the ground for the decision` IS A `Ground of the decision` @desc Why the payments are being reduced or stopped: a reduced incapacity on a health practitioner's certificate; overtime you would not have kept working; you are no longer incapacitated but have not returned to work; you failed to attend an examination or provide a certificate; you were dismissed for serious and wilful misconduct; you breached the obligation of mutuality; a s 46 review; the end of an interim seriously injured worker decision; or another ground (your consent, a return to work, the passage of time)
      `the first day of my incapacity` IS A DATE @desc The first day for which you were entitled to weekly payments (ISO 8601)
      `the day the decision takes effect` IS A DATE @desc The day the reduction or discontinuance is to take effect (ISO 8601)
GIVETH A `Notice period answer`
DECIDE `How much notice must I get before my payments change` IS
    `the s 48(6) notice for` `the ground for the decision` `with incapacity from` `the first day of my incapacity` `taking effect on` `the day the decision takes effect`

@export By when must I apply to the Tribunal, and elect, to keep my weekly payments going while I dispute a cut (s 48(9))?
GIVEN `the day I received the notice` IS A DATE @desc The day you received notice of the decision to reduce or discontinue your weekly payments (ISO 8601)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I apply to keep my payments going` IS
    `the last day to apply and elect under s 48(9) after notice received on` `the day I received the notice`

@export Does my refusal or failure breach the obligation of mutuality (s 48(3), (4))?
GIVEN `what I refused or failed to do` IS A `Refusal or failure` @desc What you refused or failed to do: reasonably refusing surgery or a drug; choosing one reasonable form of treatment over another where medical opinion differs; another refusal or failure listed in s 48(3) (an examination, a certificate, treatment, your plan, offered work, looking for work, an assessment); or none
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my refusal breach mutuality` IF
    `the worker breaches the obligation of mutuality by` `what I refused or failed to do`

@export If I win a dispute about cut payments, how much are my arrears with interest (s 48(11), (12); reg 28)?
GIVEN `the arrears` IS A NUMBER @desc The weekly payments you were not paid for one financial year, in dollars
      `the prime bank rate` IS A NUMBER @desc The prime bank rate for the financial year the arrears arose in, in per cent a year (the average of two NAB fixed rates at the start of that year, reg 3)
      `the complete weeks in arrears` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of complete weeks the amount has been in arrears
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much are my arrears with interest` IS
    `rounded half up` (`the arrears` `with reg 28 interest at` `the prime bank rate` `for` `the complete weeks in arrears`) `to` 2 `decimal places`

§§ `Lump sums for permanent impairment (ss 55-58; reg 34)`

@export What lump sum do I get for loss of future earning capacity (economic loss) (ss 55, 56; Schedules 6, 7)?
GIVEN `I am a seriously injured worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a seriously injured worker
      `I made a s 56A election` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are a seriously injured worker: whether you have elected under s 56A to receive this lump sum
      `my whole person impairment from physical injury` IS A NUMBER @desc Your degree of whole person impairment from physical injury, in per cent, as assessed under s 22
      `my injury is noise induced hearing loss` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury is noise induced hearing loss
      `I am asking for a worker who has died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker has died (a personal representative asking)
      `my final examination was on or after the 2022 designated day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the accredited medical practitioner's final examination for your assessment was on or after the designated day under the 2022 amending Act
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth (ISO 8601)
      `the day of my injury` IS A DATE @desc The day of the injury (ISO 8601)
      `the CPI for the September quarter before the adjustment` IS A NUMBER @desc The Consumer Price Index (All groups, Adelaide) for the September quarter of the year before the year of the injury
      `the CPI for the base September quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc The Consumer Price Index (All groups, Adelaide) for the September quarter of the year before the law fixing the Schedule 7 sum took effect (2014, or 2021 for a sum fixed by the 2022 amending Act)
GIVETH AN `Economic loss answer`
DECIDE `What lump sum do I get for economic loss` IS
    `the s 56 answer for`
        (`Economic loss facts` WITH
            `a seriously injured worker`                                   IS `I am a seriously injured worker`
            `made an election under s 56A`                                 IS `I made a s 56A election`
            `the whole person impairment from physical injury, in per cent` IS `my whole person impairment from physical injury`
            `the injury is noise induced hearing loss`                     IS `my injury is noise induced hearing loss`
            `the worker has died`                                          IS `I am asking for a worker who has died`
            `the final examination was on or after the 2022 designated day` IS `my final examination was on or after the 2022 designated day`
            `the age in years at the day of the injury`                    IS `the age in whole years of a person born on` `my date of birth` `on` `the day of my injury`)
        `with`
        (`CPI figures` WITH
            `the CPI for the September quarter before the adjustment` IS `the CPI for the September quarter before the adjustment`
            `the CPI for the base September quarter`                 IS `the CPI for the base September quarter`)

@export What lump sum do I get for non-economic loss (pain, suffering and loss of amenity) (ss 57, 58; reg 34)?
GIVEN `my whole person impairment from physical injury` IS A NUMBER @desc Your degree of whole person impairment from physical injury, in per cent, as assessed under s 22 (a psychiatric injury gives no lump sum)
      `I am asking for a worker who has died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker has died
      `two or more impairments were combined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether two or more impairments from the same injury or cause were combined in the assessment
      `this aggravates an injury already paid for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this injury is an aggravation, acceleration, exacerbation, deterioration or recurrence of a prior work injury for which you were already paid this lump sum
      `what I was paid before` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of that earlier lump sum, in dollars (0 if none)
      `the CPI for the latest September quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc The Consumer Price Index (All groups, Adelaide) for the September quarter of the year before the year of the injury
      `the CPI for the September quarter of 2014` IS A NUMBER @desc The Consumer Price Index (All groups, Adelaide) for the September quarter of 2014
GIVETH A `Non-economic loss answer`
DECIDE `What lump sum do I get for non-economic loss` IS
    `the s 58 answer for`
        (`Non-economic loss facts` WITH
            `the whole person impairment from physical injury, in per cent` IS `my whole person impairment from physical injury`
            `the worker has died`                                          IS `I am asking for a worker who has died`
            `two or more impairments from the same injury or cause were combined` IS `two or more impairments were combined`
            `the injury aggravates a prior work injury already paid for under s 58` IS `this aggravates an injury already paid for`
            `the previous s 58 payment`                                    IS `what I was paid before`)
        `with`
        (`CPI figures` WITH
            `the CPI for the September quarter before the adjustment` IS `the CPI for the latest September quarter`
            `the CPI for the base September quarter`                 IS `the CPI for the September quarter of 2014`)

§§ `If a worker has died of a work injury (ss 59, 61, 62; reg 35)`

-- Situation: the worker has died as a result of a work injury; asked by the partner, a child, or the person who paid for
-- the funeral.
@export Can a child of the worker who died be paid weekly payments (s 59(5))?
GIVEN `the child's age` IS A NUMBER @desc The child's age in whole years
      `the child is a full-time student` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the child is a full-time student at an educational institution approved by ReturnToWorkSA
      `the child cannot earn a living because of disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the child is, because of a physical, mental or intellectual disability, incapable of earning a living
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the child be paid weekly payments` IF
    `a child of` `the child's age` `may be paid` `the child is a full-time student` `the child cannot earn a living because of disability`

@export What weekly payment does the totally dependent partner of a worker who died get (s 59(1)(a), (7))?
GIVEN `the worker's notional weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc The notional weekly earnings of the worker who died, in dollars
      `the number of dependent children who can be paid` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of the worker's totally dependent children can be paid weekly payments (see the child question)
      `the children are orphans` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether those children are orphans: both their parents have died, or one has and they have no reasonable prospect of support from the other (for example, children of the worker whose other parent has died, where you are their step-parent)
      `the week is in the first 52 weeks` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the week falls within 52 weeks of the day the worker's incapacity first occurred
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What weekly payment does the partner get` IS
    `the s 59 weekly payment to the totally dependent spouse or domestic partner for`
        (`Death weekly payment facts` WITH
            `a totally dependent spouse or domestic partner is paid`       IS TRUE  -- the question is asked for the partner
            `the number of totally dependent children who may be paid`     IS `the number of dependent children who can be paid`
            `the children are orphaned children`                           IS `the children are orphans`
            `the notional weekly earnings of the deceased worker`          IS `the worker's notional weekly earnings`
            `the week is within 52 weeks of the first incapacity`          IS `the week is in the first 52 weeks`)

@export What weekly payment does each totally dependent child of a worker who died get (s 59(1)(b), (c), (7))?
GIVEN `the worker's notional weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc The notional weekly earnings of the worker who died, in dollars
      `a totally dependent partner survives` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a totally dependent spouse or domestic partner of the worker is also paid
      `the number of dependent children who can be paid` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of the worker's totally dependent children can be paid weekly payments (including this child)
      `the children are orphans` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the children are orphans (both parents have died, or one has and they have no reasonable prospect of support from the other)
      `the week is in the first 52 weeks` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the week falls within 52 weeks of the day the worker's incapacity first occurred
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What weekly payment does each child get` IS
    `the s 59 weekly payment to each totally dependent child for`
        (`Death weekly payment facts` WITH
            `a totally dependent spouse or domestic partner is paid`       IS `a totally dependent partner survives`
            `the number of totally dependent children who may be paid`     IS `the number of dependent children who can be paid`
            `the children are orphaned children`                           IS `the children are orphans`
            `the notional weekly earnings of the deceased worker`          IS `the worker's notional weekly earnings`
            `the week is within 52 weeks of the first incapacity`          IS `the week is in the first 52 weeks`)

@export Until what day can weekly payments be made to the family of a worker who died (s 59(6), with ss 41 and 44)?
GIVEN `the worker's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc The date of birth of the worker who died (ISO 8601)
      `the worker's kind of work had a normal retiring age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is a normal retiring age for workers in the kind of employment the worker was injured in
      `that retiring age in months` IS A NUMBER @desc That normal retiring age, in months (for example 780 for 65); 0 if none
      `the worker's age pension age in months` IS A NUMBER @desc The age, in months, at which the worker would have been eligible for the age pension under the Social Security Act 1991 (Cth) (804, which is 67, for anyone born on or after 1 January 1957)
      `the first day of the worker's incapacity` IS A DATE @desc The first day the worker was entitled to weekly payments for the injury, or, if the worker died of it without first being off work, the day of the injury (ISO 8601)
      `the worker was employed when the incapacity began` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker was still in employment when the incapacity for work first began
GIVETH A `Retiring age answer`
DECIDE `Until when can weekly payments be made after the worker's death` IS
    `the last day of s 59 weekly payments on the death of a worker with`
        (`Retiring age facts` WITH
            `the date of birth`                                           IS `the worker's date of birth`
            `there is a normal retiring age for the kind of employment`   IS `the worker's kind of work had a normal retiring age`
            `the normal retiring age, in months`                          IS `that retiring age in months`
            `the age pension age, in months`                              IS `the worker's age pension age in months`
            `the day incapacity first occurred`                           IS `the first day of the worker's incapacity`
            `still in employment when the incapacity first occurred`      IS `the worker was employed when the incapacity began`)

@export What share of the lump sum on a worker's death do the partners and children each get (s 61)?
GIVEN `the number of partners` IS A NUMBER @desc How many spouses or domestic partners the worker left (dependency is not required)
      `the number of children` IS A NUMBER @desc How many children the worker left who are under 18, or full-time students under 26, or unable to earn a living because of disability (dependency is not required)
      `the non-economic loss lump sum already paid to the worker` IS A NUMBER @desc Any lump sum for non-economic loss (Division 7) already paid to the worker for the injury, in dollars (0 if none)
      `the CPI for the latest September quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc The Consumer Price Index (All groups, Adelaide) for the September quarter of the year before the year of the injury
      `the CPI for the September quarter of 2014` IS A NUMBER @desc The Consumer Price Index (All groups, Adelaide) for the September quarter of 2014
GIVETH A `Death lump sum answer`
DECIDE `What share of the death lump sum do we get` IS
    `the s 61 shares for` `the number of partners` `partners and` `the number of children` `children of`
        (`the s 61 prescribed sum, less` `the non-economic loss lump sum already paid to the worker` `with`
            (`CPI figures` WITH
                `the CPI for the September quarter before the adjustment` IS `the CPI for the latest September quarter`
                `the CPI for the base September quarter`                 IS `the CPI for the September quarter of 2014`))

@export How much interest is added to a lump sum paid on a worker's death (s 61(11), reg 35(2))?
GIVEN `the lump sum` IS A NUMBER @desc The lump sum payable to you under s 61, in dollars
      `the prime bank rate` IS A NUMBER @desc The prime bank rate for the financial year in which the lump sum is paid, in per cent a year
      `the day the claim was lodged` IS A DATE @desc The day the claim for the lump sum was lodged (ISO 8601)
      `the day it is paid` IS A DATE @desc The day the lump sum is paid (ISO 8601)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much interest is added to the death lump sum` IS
    `rounded half up` (`the s 61(11) interest on` `the lump sum` `at` `the prime bank rate` `from` `the day the claim was lodged` `to` `the day it is paid`) `to` 2 `decimal places`

@export How much is the funeral benefit when a worker dies of a work injury (s 62, reg 35(3))?
GIVEN `the actual cost of the funeral` IS A NUMBER @desc What the worker's funeral actually cost, in dollars
      `the CPI for the latest September quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc The Consumer Price Index (All groups, Adelaide) for the September quarter of the year before the year of the injury
      `the CPI for the September quarter of 2014` IS A NUMBER @desc The Consumer Price Index (All groups, Adelaide) for the September quarter of 2014
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much is the funeral benefit` IS
    `the funeral benefit for a funeral costing` `the actual cost of the funeral` `with`
        (`CPI figures` WITH
            `the CPI for the September quarter before the adjustment` IS `the CPI for the latest September quarter`
            `the CPI for the base September quarter`                 IS `the CPI for the September quarter of 2014`)

§§ `Suing my employer, and challenging a decision (ss 72, 100)`

@export May damages be awarded against my employer for my work injury (s 72)?
GIVEN `my whole person impairment from physical injury` IS A NUMBER @desc Your degree of permanent impairment from physical injury, in per cent, as assessed under s 22 or Part 8 (0 if none)
      `my whole person impairment from psychiatric injury` IS A NUMBER @desc Your degree of permanent impairment from psychiatric injury, in per cent, assessed separately (0 if none)
      `my final examination was on or after the 2022 designated day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the accredited medical practitioner's final examination for your assessment was on or after the designated day under the 2022 amending Act
      `I am asking about a worker who died of the injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker died as a result of the injury
GIVETH A `Damages answer`
DECIDE `May I sue my employer` IS
    `the s 72 answer for`
        (`Impairment facts` WITH
            `the whole person impairment from physical injury, in per cent`     IS `my whole person impairment from physical injury`
            `the whole person impairment from psychiatric injury, in per cent`  IS `my whole person impairment from psychiatric injury`
            `the final examination was on or after the 2022 designated day`     IS `my final examination was on or after the 2022 designated day`)
        `with death` `I am asking about a worker who died of the injury`

@export By when must I apply to the Tribunal for review of a decision (s 100(1))?
GIVEN `the day I received notice of the decision` IS A DATE @desc The day you received notice of the decision you want reviewed (ISO 8601)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I apply to the Tribunal` IS
    `the last day to apply to the Tribunal after notice received on` `the day I received notice of the decision`

@export I am out of time: may the Tribunal extend my time to apply (s 100(2))?
GIVEN `the Tribunal is satisfied there is good reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal is satisfied that good reason exists for the delay
      `the Tribunal is satisfied no one is unreasonably disadvantaged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal is satisfied that no other party will be unreasonably disadvantaged by the delay
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Tribunal extend my time` IF
    `the Tribunal may extend the time` `the Tribunal is satisfied there is good reason` `the Tribunal is satisfied no one is unreasonably disadvantaged`

§§ `Indexed amounts (s 4(17); regs 4, 8)`

@export What is an amount marked "(indexed)" in the Act or regulations worth this year (s 4(17), regs 4 and 8)?
GIVEN `the amount as stated` IS A NUMBER @desc The dollar amount as written in the Act or regulations, before indexation
      `the CPI for the latest September quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc The Consumer Price Index (All groups, Adelaide) for the September quarter of last year
      `the CPI for the base September quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc The same index for the September quarter of 2014 for an amount in the regulations, or, for an amount in the Act, of the year before the law fixing it took effect
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the indexed amount` IS
    `the amount as stated` `indexed by`
        (`CPI figures` WITH
            `the CPI for the September quarter before the adjustment` IS `the CPI for the latest September quarter`
            `the CPI for the base September quarter`                 IS `the CPI for the base September quarter`)
